#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Regression check of every live entry through the :8080 gateway against stored golden outputs (2026-11-17).

  bin/regress --record [--only PAT]   (re)write the golden outputs from the current deployment
  bin/regress --quick                 one fixed request per entry (after every change)
  bin/regress                         full set (after big changes: MLX / env / engine upgrades, directory moves)
  options: --only LIST (comma list of exact case ids or model ids; "embed-*" matches a prefix), --no-lock (caller already holds the gpu-lock and
           has llama-swap running), --list

Every request is deterministic (temperature 0 / fixed seed). Comparison per kind:
  chat      temp-0 text byte-identical                                        else FAIL
  embed     identical vectors -> PASS; min cosine >= 0.9999 -> WARN           else FAIL
  rerank    identical scores -> PASS; same order and max diff <= 0.01 -> WARN else FAIL
  decide    identical probabilities -> PASS; same top answers, max |dp| <= 0.01 -> WARN; else FAIL
  asr       transcript identical                                              else FAIL
  tts       audio bytes identical -> PASS; duration within 10 % and the same qwen3-asr transcript -> WARN; else FAIL
  image     identical pixels -> PASS; PSNR >= 40 dB -> WARN                    else FAIL
  video     MP4 bytes identical -> PASS; ffmpeg PSNR >= 40 dB -> WARN         else FAIL
  smoke     request succeeds with the expected fields (non-deterministic paths such as prompt_enhance=llm)
Speed (2026-11-18): chat / embed / rerank / decide / asr cases are sent a second time and that warm time is kept as
meta.json "warm_seconds" (stored by --record, or by the first passing run when missing). A later warm time above
SLOWER x that (and at least SLOWER_MIN_S more) turns PASS into WARN "slower", so speed regressions show up too;
the decide-long-* cases (32K / 16K tokens) exist for this.
Entries missing from /v1/models are SKIPped. Archived entries (2026-11-23, user rule) are SKIP(archived) and get no
request at all, so a regression run never makes bin/archive-restore copy weights back from the Mac mini: an entry is
archived when one of the ~/models directories its llama-swap cmd passes to archive-restore (--model A --model B) has
a manifest ~/models/<dir>.archive and the local copy is missing or incomplete (archive-restore's own load_manifest /
problems checks). The summary counts PASS / WARN / FAIL / SKIP / SKIP(archived) separately; --list shows them too.
Golden outputs: evals/golden/<case>/ or $LLM_GOLDEN_DIR (input copies,
golden.*, meta.json; recorded on each machine with --record, never committed). Results: logs/regress/<time>.{txt,json}; exit 1 if anything FAILed.

GPU: unless --no-lock, the run takes the whole gpu-lock pool as "regress" (retrying exit 1, giving up on exit 4),
resumes llama-swap (gpu-lock pauses it for the first holder) so requests are served through it as for clients, and
releases the lock on exit. Models are loaded by llama-swap's own servers, so memguard has nothing to wrap here.
Cases run in an order that keeps model swaps low: resident and coexisting entries first, exclusive ones last.
"""

import os
import sys
from pathlib import Path

# Run with the deployment's Python environment (<checkout>/.venv) whatever python3 the shebang found.
_VENV = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / ".venv"
if Path(sys.prefix).resolve() != _VENV.resolve() and (_VENV / "bin/python").is_file():
    os.execv(str(_VENV / "bin/python"), [str(_VENV / "bin/python"), __file__, *sys.argv[1:]])

import argparse
